      {
        "id": "kill_instruction",
        "kind": "engine",
        "engine": "util",
        "operation": "template",
        "params": {
          "template": "The text is the OCR of the kill feed (top-right corner) of a Valorant or CS2 gameplay recording, sampled once per second and read in blocks of 10 seconds. Blocks are separated by ###. Inside a block, each frame starts with a line \"TS <seconds>\", the time of that frame in the video (OCR may read the digit 0 as the letter O), followed by the kill-feed rows at that moment, until the next TS line. Only blocks where the player's name appears are included. The player's name is: {{a}} (OCR may misread a few letters, e.g. 0/O, 1/l/I, 5/S, 8/B).\nIn each kill-feed row the killer is written first and the victim second. A row where the player's name comes second is the player dying: ignore it. A row stays on screen for about 5 seconds, so the same kill appears in several consecutive frames: count it once.\nTask: list every kill by the player. A kill moment K is the first second a new row with the player as killer appears: either the number of rows with the player as killer goes up, or such a row reappears after a gap of more than 2 seconds. When several new rows appear at once, list each kill with the same K.\nAnswer exactly in this shape: {\"kills\":[{\"t\":number}],\"totalKills\":integer}, with t in seconds, in time order. If there are no kills, answer {\"kills\":[],\"totalKills\":0}."
        },
        "position": {
          "x": 1800,
          "y": 180
        }
      },
